1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Ainize.ai: sign in with a real MetaMask wallet.
This recording will compare the same model before and after loading trained memory.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Review the actual Ainize sign-in challenge in MetaMask.
This is authentication only: no funds move and no spending is approved.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Open Live Test, then the working question link from the repository README.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The Graph lesson: ask the token symbol of the README's ERC-4626 vault.
Compare mode unloads the selected knowledge for Before, then loads it for After.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:20,000
BEFORE: yvUSDC. AFTER: G-UNI, matching the lesson's expected answer.
These are actual model replies, not a Graph lookup supplied as answer context.

6
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Second README example: what is this vault's performance fee?
The same selected memory patch is tested in both columns.

7
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:56,000
BEFORE: 10%. AFTER: 2.5%, matching the published lesson.
Each column keeps its own history; the base does not receive the patched answer.

8
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Switch to the knowledge named defi.engram.eth: Messari vocabulary.
Ask what the Lending Market field rates means.

9
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Before: a general interest-rate explanation. After: the taught schema wording.
This shows a specific memory response, not proof that the whole base answer is false.

10
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Separately, resolve patch.ainize-4782c76e.eth on canonical Sepolia ENS.
The answer reports the node, linked dataset and actual REJECTED patch status.

11
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:25,000
The live ENS answer includes its source block and result hash.
This last panel uses live source grounding; the earlier side-by-side tests use memory.

12
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Observed examples, not a claim of universal accuracy or a fresh training run.
The lesson's locality limitations and reproduction evidence are in the repository.
